        "original_id": "b89aa061-0818-5cd1-858d-a36a6fca4813",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- People: Charlie Ross, Gregg Harper, Tom Harkin, George Miller\n- Places: Mississippi's 3rd congressional district, Rankin County\n- Roles: U.S. Representative, Republican Chairman, Senate committee chair, House committee ranking member\n- Organizations: Senate Health, Education, Labor, and Pensions Committee, House Education and Workforce Committee\n- Legislation: Keeping All Students Safe Act\n\nFacts:\n- Gregory Livingston Harper was born on June 1, 1956.\n- In 2008, Charlie Ross ran for Congress in Mississippi's 3rd congressional district and lost the Republican primary to Rankin County Republican Chairman Gregg Harper.\n- Since 2009, Gregg Harper has served as the U.S. Representative for Mississippi's 3rd congressional district.\n- Senator Tom Harkin chaired the Senate Health, Education, Labor, and Pensions Committee when he was a primary sponsor of the Keeping All Students Safe Act.\n- Congressman George Miller was the Ranking Member of the House Education and Workforce Committee when he was a primary sponsor of the Keeping All Students Safe Act.\n- Congressman Gregg Harper was also a primary sponsor of the Keeping All Students Safe Act.",
        "type": "TextSummary"
      },
